diff --git a/install/omarchy-aarch64-google.packages b/install/omarchy-aarch64-google.packages
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..db0b0d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/install/omarchy-aarch64-google.packages
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Google Chrome OS (aarch64-google) additions, composed after
+# omarchy-base.packages and omarchy-aarch64.packages. The kernel and the signed
+# depthcharge boot chain come with the image (the kernel travels as a [platform]
+# bundle), not from here; a device cannot work without the packages below.
+
+# Chrome OS boot tooling. `vboot-utils` provides cgpt, crossystem and futility
+# together, and `depthcharge-tools` provides depthchargectl, which builds the
+# signed FIT written to the kernel partition.
+vboot-utils
+depthcharge-tools
+
+# The Chromebook action row has no F1-F10; keyd supplies them.
+keyd
+
+# The MT8192 sound card is only usable once its ALSA UCM boot sequence has run
+# (alsa-utils), and ALSA-only applications need PipeWire's default PCM.
+alsa-ucm-conf
+alsa-utils
+pipewire-alsa
+
+# Firmware split by vendor in Arch Linux ARM: MediaTek (SCP) and Realtek
+# (RTW88 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth).
+linux-firmware-mediatek
+linux-firmware-realtek
+
+# The platform implementation itself: the keyd map, the brightness rule and the
+# platform data the shell reads, which upstream keeps out of the shell and in a
+# platform repository (Apple's omarchy-mac-pkgs is the model). Its boot half,
+# omarchy-google-boot, joins this list with the boot chain.
+omarchy-google
